CAT = "aurcgEnv"; SEG = "ENV"
Q = [
('Why should clocks showing the correct time be visible in gaming areas?',
 'So players notice time passing', ['So staff can time their breaks', 'So machines stay in sync', 'So the venue closes on time'],
 'Gaming areas often have no windows or clocks, so players lose track of time. Visible, correct clocks are one of the harm minimisation strategies in the national unit.'),
('Where should ATMs be placed under the harm minimisation principles in the unit?',
 'Outside the gaming area', ['Next to the machines', "At the cashier's desk", 'Just inside the gaming room'],
 'Keeping ATMs out of gaming areas puts distance between the player and more cash, giving them a chance to stop and think.'),
('Venue ATM facilities should not allow cash withdrawals from:',
 'Credit accounts', ['Savings accounts', 'Cheque accounts', 'Debit card accounts'],
 'The unit lists blocking cash withdrawals from credit accounts as a harm minimisation principle, so players do not gamble with borrowed money.'),
('Where should gambling-related signage, such as promotions for gaming machines, be kept?',
 'Inside the venue', ['Facing the street', 'On roadside billboards', 'On bus shelters nearby'],
 'Containing gambling signage inside the venue, and not advertising gaming machines, are harm minimisation principles in the unit. Exact advertising rules vary by state.'),
('Advertising gaming machines to the public is:',
 'Restricted', ['Encouraged', 'Required', 'Unregulated'],
 'The unit lists not publishing gaming machine advertising as a harm minimisation principle. Many states ban or tightly restrict it; details vary.'),
('Which sign must be displayed where players can see it?',
 'Gambling help service details', ["Last week's jackpot winners", 'A list of the hottest machines', 'The staff rosters for the week'],
 'Venues must display information about counselling and support services, such as the Gambling Help line, where players can see it. The exact wording and placement vary by state.'),
('What should signs about the chances of winning tell players?',
 'The real odds of winning', ['Which machine is due', 'How to beat the machines', 'When jackpots usually pay'],
 'Chances of winning signage and player information explain the real odds and how machines work, so players can make informed choices.'),
('Which strategy encourages players to take breaks in play?',
 'Reminders and session alerts', ['Free credits for staying longer', 'Removing all clocks', 'Bringing drinks to the machine'],
 'Reminders, pop-up messages and alerts about time and spending encourage breaks. Free credits and constant service at the machine do the opposite.'),
('Offering free drinks to keep a customer playing the machines is:',
 'An inducement to gamble', ['Good customer service', 'Required by law', 'A harm minimisation step'],
 'Rewards that encourage people to keep gambling are inducements and are banned or restricted by codes of practice in many states.'),
('Lighting and natural light in a gaming area help responsible gambling because they:',
 'Help players track the time', ['Make the machines sound louder', 'Increase the size of bets', 'Hide the exits from players'],
 'Dark rooms without windows make it easy to lose track of time. Natural light and visible clocks remind people how long they have played.'),
('Where must self-exclusion information be available?',
 'Where players can access it', ["Only in the manager's office", 'Only on request by phone', 'Only after closing'],
 'Information about self-exclusion programs should be visible or easy to get in the gaming area and at the venue, as signage and brochures, according to state requirements.'),
('Gaming machine warning notices should be placed:',
 'On or near each machine', ['Only at the entrance', 'Only in the staff areas', 'Out in the car park'],
 'Warning and player information notices are displayed on or next to machines so players see them while they play. Exact requirements vary by state.'),
('A promotion offers double points for playing the pokies past midnight. Under responsible gambling principles this is:',
 'A risky inducement', ['Good marketing', 'A break in play', 'A harm reduction tool'],
 'Rewards that encourage longer or later play push people to gamble more. Codes of practice in many states restrict such loyalty promotions.'),
('A customer asks for change for the gaming machines with a credit card. What should you do?',
 'Refuse and explain the policy', ['Process it quickly for them', 'Process it and charge a fee', 'Ask a manager to approve it'],
 'Credit cards must not be used to fund venue gambling under harm minimisation rules. Explain politely why it cannot be done.'),
('Why is information on support services often printed on small contact cards?',
 'So help can be taken discreetly', ["To advertise the venue's bistro", "To record the player's wins", "To track members' spending"],
 'Contact cards let a person take help line details privately without drawing attention, which respects their confidentiality.'),
('Which feature of a gaming area best supports responsible gambling?',
 'Visible clocks and help signs', ['No windows and no clocks', 'An ATM beside the machines', 'Free drinks served at machines'],
 'Visible clocks and help information support informed choices. The other options keep people playing longer or give easier access to more cash.'),
('Who is responsible for keeping responsible gambling signs in place during a shift?',
 'Staff, within their duties', ['Only the state regulator', 'Only the customers', 'Only the cleaning contractor'],
 'The unit expects staff to ensure environmental features, including signage, support responsible gambling within their own role, and to report missing or damaged signs.'),
('You notice the gambling help sign near the machines is missing. What should you do?',
 'Report it so it is replaced', ['Leave it until an inspection', 'Remove the others to match', 'Write your own sign'],
 'Required signage must stay in place. Report it to your supervisor so the correct approved sign can be replaced quickly.'),
('Responsible gambling signs and notices should be written in:',
 'Approved, plain wording', ['Any wording staff like', 'Very small print only', 'Code words for staff only'],
 'Signs use wording set or approved under state rules and should be clear and easy to read. Exact wording varies by state.'),
('A player loyalty program that shows members their spending and time played can help by:',
 'Making spending visible', ["Hiding a player's losses", 'Increasing bet sizes', 'Removing spending limits'],
 'Activity statements and spending information help players see how much time and money they have really spent, which supports informed choices.'),
('Pre-commitment in gambling means:',
 'Setting limits before playing', ['Paying for credits in advance', 'Booking a favourite machine', 'Promising to come back later'],
 'Pre-commitment lets a player set time or money limits before they start. Some states have pre-commitment systems on gaming machines; details vary by state.'),
('Why are ATMs kept away from gaming machines?',
 'To create a pause before more cash', ['To speed up cash withdrawals', 'To save floor space for seating', 'To reduce noise from the machines'],
 'Distance between the machines and cash gives the player a moment to reconsider before spending more.'),
('Which is an example of a strategy that indicates the passage of time?',
 'Visible clocks in the gaming area', ['Machines with no time display', 'Blacked-out windows in the room', 'Loud music played constantly'],
 'The unit requires evidence of strategies that indicate the passage of time, such as visible clocks and time-of-day reminders.'),
('Serving food and drinks to customers at the machine can work against breaks in play because:',
 'Players never need to stop', ['It raises the odds of winning', 'It is illegal in every state', 'It lowers the return to player'],
 'If everything is brought to the machine the player never has to get up. Some states restrict service at machines; check your state rules.'),
('Which statement about promotional material in gaming areas is correct?',
 'It must follow state rules', ['It can promise players wins', 'It can be aimed at minors', 'It never needs any approval'],
 'Promotions must not mislead about chances of winning, target minors or encourage excessive play, and they must follow state advertising and code of practice rules.'),
('Which of these is a harm minimisation measure in the gaming environment?',
 'Limits on cash access', ['Free play for heavy losers', 'Extended opening hours', 'Credit for members'],
 'Limiting easy access to cash, such as keeping ATMs out of gaming areas and blocking credit withdrawals, is a core harm minimisation measure.'),
('Why might a venue display a list of local counselling services in toilets as well as gaming areas?',
 'So people can read it privately', ['To meet the cleaning rules', 'To advertise the bar menu', 'To fill some empty wall space'],
 'Some people prefer to read help information where no one is watching. Displaying it in private spaces makes it easier to seek help.'),
('A gaming machine shows a pop-up message about how long the person has been playing. This is an example of:',
 'A player information message', ['A fault in the machine', 'A bonus game feature', 'A linked jackpot alert'],
 'Pop-up messages on time played or money spent are harm minimisation features that encourage players to pause and reconsider. Their use varies by state.'),
('Whether gaming machines must close for a few hours each night (a shutdown period) is set by:',
 'State law', ['The customers', 'The machine supplier', "The venue's cleaners"],
 'Many states require gaming machines to shut down for a set period each day, but the hours vary by state and sometimes by venue type.'),
("A customer asks if they can have a drink brought to them so they don't lose their machine. A responsible reply is to:",
 'Suggest a short break', ['Hold the machine all night', 'Bring drinks every hour', 'Give free credits instead'],
 'Encouraging a break supports responsible gambling. Follow your venue policy and state rules on service at machines.'),
("Children's play areas located where children can see into the gaming room are:",
 'Not appropriate', ['Recommended for families', 'Required by law', 'Good for business'],
 'Minors must not be in gaming areas, and venues should keep children away from and out of sight of gambling activity where state rules require it.'),
("A sign telling players to 'Chase your luck tonight' would be:",
 'Against responsible gambling', ['Good customer service', 'A notice required by law', 'An approved help service sign'],
 'Messages that encourage chasing or excessive play conflict with responsible gambling principles and codes of practice.'),
]
